<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_4_2" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_4_2" name="4.2 Prepare, perform and complete the work" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>4.2.1, 4.2.2, 4.2.3, 4.2.4 and 4.2.6 are drawn; 4.2.5 is a case with its own file. This is the spine of the category and, with 4.4, the most heavily evidenced path in the model.

TWO STOPS ARE DRAWN AS STOPS RATHER THAN AS DECISIONS. 4.2.1 refers a missing or conflicting prerequisite and does not proceed - it does not obtain the permit, which is 2.6, and it does not issue the clearance, which is 18.4.4. And 4.2.3 stops when scope, safety or operating state is no longer valid, handing to 4.2.5 rather than pressing on. Both are the difference between a model of what should happen and a model of what does.

The safety assessment repeats. 29 CFR 1910.269(c)(3)(ii) requires an additional job briefing where there is a significant change affecting employee safety, so 4.2.2 is re-entered from 4.2.3 rather than being a gate passed once at the start.

4.2.4 SUBMITS actuals; it does not close anything. 5.1 closes the work order, and the boundary is drawn so that field completion and administrative closure are visibly two events.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_4_2_lanes">
      <lane id="l_42_crew" name="Field crew">
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_rev</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_pre</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_ok</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_ref</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_jsa</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_area</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_do</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_mon</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_chg</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_susp</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_res</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_act</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_sub</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_chk</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_temp</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_rel</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_42_end</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_42_start" name="Crew on site with an assigned work package"><messageEventDefinition id="n_42_start_md"/></startEvent>
    <userTask id="n_42_rev" name="Review scope, method, location and asset identity"><documentation>4.2.1. Asset identity included - the commonest field failure is correct work on the wrong asset.</documentation></userTask>
    <userTask id="n_42_pre" name="Confirm permits, materials, equipment and qualifications"><documentation>4.2.1. And the approved switching or outage condition where one applies.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_42_ok" name="Prerequisites complete"/>
    <sendTask id="n_42_ref" name="Stop and refer the missing prerequisite"><documentation>4.2.1. Referred, not obtained. A permit is 2.6; a clearance is 18.4.4; neither is this crew's to create.</documentation></sendTask>
    <userTask id="n_42_jsa" name="Perform the pre-job safety assessment and briefing"><documentation>4.2.2. Hazards, energy sources, roles, qualifications, emergency arrangements, controls - then the briefing. 4.4.1 is the tailboard record.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_42_area" name="Establish the controlled work area"><documentation>4.2.3.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_42_do" name="Perform tasks in the authorised sequence"><documentation>4.2.3. Authorised sequence - for work under a clearance that sequence is 1910.269(m)(3)'s and is not the crew's to reorder.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_42_mon" name="Scope, safety and operating state still valid"/>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_42_chg" name="Change is material"/>
    <callActivity id="n_42_susp" name="Suspend, transfer or escalate (4.2.5)"><documentation>4.2.5. A case. Stopping is the correct outcome and the model draws it as one.</documentation></callActivity>
    <userTask id="n_42_res" name="Confirm the physical task result"><documentation>4.2.3.</documentation></userTask>
    <userTask id="n_42_act" name="Record tasks, labour, materials, tools and vehicles"><documentation>4.2.4. With exceptions and follow-up.</documentation></userTask>
    <sendTask id="n_42_sub" name="Submit the field actuals"><documentation>4.2.4. Submitted. 5.1 closes the work order; this is not that event.</documentation></sendTask>
    <userTask id="n_42_chk" name="Confirm every task complete or dispositioned"><documentation>4.2.6. Dispositioned counts - a task deliberately not done, recorded as such, is a complete package.</documentation></userTask>
    <userTask id="n_42_temp" name="Verify temporary protections and restoration status"><documentation>4.2.6. What 4.6 will inherit, including anything left temporary.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_42_rel" name="Release tools, crew and local controls"><documentation>4.2.6.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <endEvent id="n_42_end" name="Field work complete"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_start_n_42_rev" sourceRef="n_42_start" targetRef="n_42_rev" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_rev_n_42_pre" sourceRef="n_42_rev" targetRef="n_42_pre" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_pre_n_42_ok" sourceRef="n_42_pre" targetRef="n_42_ok" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_ok_n_42_ref" sourceRef="n_42_ok" targetRef="n_42_ref" name="missing or conflicting"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[prerequisitesComplete = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_ok_n_42_jsa" sourceRef="n_42_ok" targetRef="n_42_jsa" name="complete"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_jsa_n_42_area" sourceRef="n_42_jsa" targetRef="n_42_area" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_area_n_42_do" sourceRef="n_42_area" targetRef="n_42_do" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_do_n_42_mon" sourceRef="n_42_do" targetRef="n_42_mon" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_mon_n_42_chg" sourceRef="n_42_mon" targetRef="n_42_chg" name="conditions changed"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[stillValid = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_chg_n_42_jsa" sourceRef="n_42_chg" targetRef="n_42_jsa" name="significant change affecting safety - rebrief under (c)(3)(ii)"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_chg_n_42_susp" sourceRef="n_42_chg" targetRef="n_42_susp" name="cannot continue"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_mon_n_42_res" sourceRef="n_42_mon" targetRef="n_42_res" name="still valid"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_res_n_42_act" sourceRef="n_42_res" targetRef="n_42_act" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_act_n_42_sub" sourceRef="n_42_act" targetRef="n_42_sub" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_sub_n_42_chk" sourceRef="n_42_sub" targetRef="n_42_chk" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_chk_n_42_temp" sourceRef="n_42_chk" targetRef="n_42_temp" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_temp_n_42_rel" sourceRef="n_42_temp" targetRef="n_42_rel" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_42_rel_n_42_end" sourceRef="n_42_rel" targetRef="n_42_end" name=""/>
  </process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="dg_P_4_2">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="pl_P_4_2" bpmnElement="P_4_2">
